  "body": "What the user asked for (chat, 2026-11-14): \"i want it to form a smooth link move over holes in the surface. lets start with a straight line between each edge of the hole. later we can add splines and curves for how to connect them.\"\n\nWhat happens now: finish3d (Parallel and the other march patterns) breaks a raster line where the tool cannot stand, for example over a hole. The chain between the two runs lifts to the retract plane. The tool makes an air hop for every gap. On a part with many holes this is slow and the moves look wrong in the GUI.\n\nChange: add an operation parameter `gap_link` to the finishing parameters. The parameter is a dropdown with two options:\n\n- `Jump` (default): today's behaviour, unchanged. The chain lifts to the retract plane.\n- `Straight`: one straight Feed move between the end of one run and the start of the next, at the two end points' own tip height.\n\nLaw for `Straight`: both run ends stand at tangent centers by the march construction. The author certifies the exact segment-triangle sweep of the move at the budget `r - TOUCH_EPS`. A grazing contact at the rim passes. A real bite refuses. On a refusal the chain takes the `Jump` hop. No air margin is added for `Straight`; `Jump` keeps its own retract law.\n\nAlso fixed, needed by this feature: the raster serpentine ran a broken back line wrong. It reversed only each piece's points and kept the pieces in grid order. Every gap link then jumped back across the field instead of crossing its gap. A back line now reverses whole: the pieces in reverse order, and each piece's points reversed. This also shortens the existing `Jump` traverses on broken lines.\n\nHow the parameter is stored: the project digest takes a `0x4D` tag plus a variant byte only when `gap_link` is not `Jump`. The project file grammar takes the words `jump` and `straight`. No project-file version step-up. The MCP params door and the UI combo carry the same two options.\n\nDone means:\n\n- The Gap link dropdown offers Jump and Straight; Jump is the default and writes the old bytes.\n- Over a holed plate, `Straight` authors rim-to-rim Feed links at the run height and no retract hop for those gaps.\n- A `Straight` link that would cut the part is refused, and the hop stands (Prime Directive).\n- Every gap crossing on a broken back line spans one gap, never the field.\n- Pins: `crates/motion/tests/finish3d_gaplink.rs`, the round-trip pins in `crates/app/tests/project_roundtrip.rs`, and the MCP params-door test.\n",
